<BaseLayout title="Food assistance in Sandusky and the Firelands" description={description}>
  <article class="wrap guide">
    <p><a href="/links">Community links</a> / Local guides</p>
    <h1>Food assistance in Sandusky and the Firelands</h1>
    <p class="lede">Find a pantry, check who it serves and learn what to bring before making the trip.</p>
    <p>Provider websites checked <time datetime="2026-11-15">Nov. 15, 2026</time>. We review this guide monthly and when a change is reported. Next review: Dec. 15, 2026.</p>
    <p>This is a starting point, not a complete directory. Hours below are local Eastern time. Call before traveling, especially around holidays or severe weather, to confirm that day's service, food availability, documents and any appointment requirement. A pantry's rules apply only to that provider.</p>
    <nav aria-label="In this guide"><a href="#sandusky">Sandusky</a> · <a href="#regional">Erie and Huron county food search</a> · <a href="#fremont">Fremont</a> · <a href="#ottawa">Ottawa County</a> · <a href="#benefits">Food benefits and more locations</a></nav>

    <h2 id="sandusky">Care &amp; Share of Erie County, Sandusky</h2>
    <p><strong>Where:</strong> 241 Jackson St., Sandusky. <strong>Phone:</strong> <a href="tel:+14196241411">419-624-1411</a>.</p>
    <p>The provider's <a href="https://careandshareerieco.org/hours/">eligibility and client-hours page</a> lists these food and clothing pantry hours:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Monday, Tuesday and Thursday: 9–10:45 a.m. and 1–2:45 p.m.</li>
      <li>Tuesday evening: 5–6:45 p.m.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Who qualifies:</strong> Erie County, Ohio residents who meet Ohio Department of Job and Family Services / The Emergency Food Assistance Program income guidelines.</p>
    <p><strong>What to bring:</strong> Picture identification for each household member age 18 or older. If your ID does not show your current address, bring mail proving Erie County residency. Bring identification for children under 18, such as a birth certificate, medical card, Social Security card or another form of ID. Ask the pantry about alternatives if you are missing documents. The website's separate donation hours are not client-service hours.</p>

    <h2 id="regional">Find food in Erie and Huron counties with Second Harvest</h2>
    <p><a href="https://www.secondharvestfoodbank.org/about/about-us-1">Second Harvest Food Bank of North Central Ohio</a> serves Erie, Huron, Lorain and Crawford counties through its partner network. Call <a href="tel:+14409602265">440-960-2265</a> for help finding a program.</p>
    <p>Use the <a href="https://www.secondharvestfoodbank.org/find-help">provider's Find Help page</a> to reach its FreshTrak search for nearby pantries and meal sites. Its <a href="https://www.secondharvestfoodbank.org/find-help/drive-thru-mobile-pantry">mobile pantry calendar</a> lists individual locations, dates, times and registration links. Check the specific occurrence; a past distribution does not establish next month's date, and special distributions may require registration.</p>
    <p><strong>Eligibility:</strong> Second Harvest says households must meet its <a href="https://www.secondharvestfoodbank.org/find-help/eligibility-for-food">income eligibility guidelines</a>, but do not have to show proof of income at its distributions or partner food pantries. Ask about current household-size limits and the selected site's other requirements before going; this does not remove another pantry's ID or residency rules.</p>
    <p>For drive-through distributions, clear space in your trunk. If collecting for another household, follow the provider's linked proxy-form instructions. Call Second Harvest to ask about access if you cannot use a drive-through service.</p>

    <h2 id="fremont">Sandusky County Food Pantry, Fremont</h2>
    <p><strong>Where:</strong> 129 Bidwell Ave., at the rear of the Share &amp; Care building, Fremont. <strong>Phone:</strong> <a href="tel:+14193348158">419-334-8158</a>; leave a message.</p>
    <p>The pantry's <a href="https://sanduskycountyfoodpantry.org/HoursLocation.html">hours and location page</a> lists noon–2:30 p.m. Monday–Thursday, closed on holidays and during Level 2 or Level 3 snow emergencies.</p>
    <p><strong>Who qualifies:</strong> Its <a href="https://sanduskycountyfoodpantry.org/Receive_Aid.html">receiving-aid page</a> says clients must live in Sandusky County and present a photo ID. Help is available once every 30 days; referrals are no longer required. Call about any additional intake requirements. This pantry serves Sandusky County, a different county from the city of Sandusky in Erie County.</p>

    <h2 id="ottawa">Ottawa County pantries</h2>
    <h3>BCS Food Pantry, Oak Harbor</h3>
    <p><strong>Where:</strong> St. Paul United Church of Christ, 165 N. Toussaint St., Oak Harbor. <strong>Phone:</strong> <a href="tel:+14198980852">419-898-0852</a>, option 2.</p>
    <p>The <a href="https://www.stpauluccoh.org/bcs-food-pantry/">church's pantry page</a> says it serves residents of the Benton-Carroll-Salem school district and opens Monday and Thursday, 8:30–11:30 a.m. Its <a href="https://www.stpauluccoh.org/">homepage</a> limits visits to once a month. The pantry page does not specify income limits or required documents; call to confirm eligibility, what to bring and holiday arrangements.</p>

    <h3>St. Vincent de Paul Food Pantry, Port Clinton</h3>
    <p><strong>Where:</strong> 129 Maple St., Port Clinton. <strong>Phone:</strong> <a href="tel:+14197344004">419-734-4004</a>.</p>
    <p>The <a href="https://www.svdpfoodpntry.org/home">pantry's website</a> says it serves people living in the Port Clinton school district who meet State of Ohio income requirements. Distribution is every other Thursday, 4–5:30 p.m.; check its calendar for the actual dates. Ask the pantry which documents and forms are needed and whether your household qualifies before visiting.</p>

    <h2 id="benefits">Food benefits and more locations</h2>
    <p>For ongoing food-benefit help, contact your county Job and Family Services agency. <a href="https://sanduskycountydjfs.org/public/food-assistance/">Sandusky County Job and Family Services</a> explains Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP) applications and local referrals. The agency determines eligibility through an application and interview; pantry eligibility does not establish SNAP eligibility.</p>
    <p>Sandusky County residents needing emergency food assistance can contact the agency at <a href="tel:+14193343891">419-334-3891</a> or visit 2511 Countryside Drive, Suite A, Fremont, Monday–Friday, 8 a.m.–4:30 p.m., closed holidays. The agency says it may be able to provide expedited benefits or a pantry referral; same-day benefits are not guaranteed. Its food-assistance page also lists additional local pantries and served meals. Confirm the details with the individual provider.</p>
    <p>Found a changed schedule, service area or requirement? <a href="/contact">Tell Firelands Current</a> so we can check with the provider and update this guide. For help with food, contact the providers above directly.</p>
  </article>
